<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>netstandard2.0</TargetFramework>
    <IncludeBuildOutput>false</IncludeBuildOutput>
    <GenerateDependencyFile>false</GenerateDependencyFile>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);NU5128;NU5100</NoWarn>
    <PackageId>TINS.Native.Desktop</PackageId>
    <Description>Meta-package bundling TINS.Native.win-x64, TINS.Native.linux-x64, TINS.Native.osx-x64, and TINS.Native.osx-arm64, so a multi-platform consumer (e.g. a cross-targeted test project) can pull in native OpenBLAS/PocketFFT assets for every desktop RID with a single reference instead of adding each RID package individually. A single-RID deployment should still reference just its own TINS.Native.&lt;rid&gt; package directly -- this carries no native content of its own. FFTW is not included here, per the FFTW/core license split (GPL-2.0-or-later vs. BSD-3-Clause) -- see TINS.Native.FFTW.Desktop for the equivalent opt-in bundle.</Description>
    <PackageTags>Neuroscience, Native, OpenBLAS, PocketFFT, Desktop</PackageTags>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- $(Version) isn't usable here: MinVer computes it via a build target that runs *after*
         restore, but restore needs a concrete version immediately (fails with NU1102
         otherwise). So these are hand-pinned floors instead; plain (non-floating,
         non-bracketed) version strings, which NuGet treats as minimum-inclusive bounds
         (">= X"), not exact pins.

         Condensed history (see CLAUDE.md's Decision 8/9 for the full blow-by-blow of every
         iteration, including exact dates/commits):
         - A floating version or an abstract/height-less floor both caused real problems
           (silently ratcheting minimums, or permanent NU1603 noise on every single restore;
           reported for real by a downstream consumer, AxoSync). Settled on pinning to a real,
           concrete, currently-valid version instead.
         - osx-x64 was dropped entirely on 2026-09-24 when it was excluded from the CI matrix
           (no package existed for this reference to point at); re-added below on 2026-10-15
           once it had a real build again.
         - v1.0.0 (2026-09-24) shipped this floor stale, pointing at a pre-release height that
           had never actually been published; permanent NU1603 warnings for every consumer
           until v1.0.1 fixed it. That incident is why the "Verify Desktop dependency floors
           are actually published" CI step exists now (see ci.yml's pack-desktop job); it
           fails the build loudly if this floor (or the matching one in
           TINS.Native.FFTW.Desktop.csproj) is ever left stale again, instead of silently
           shipping a bad reference. -->
    <PackageReference Include="TINS.Native.win-x64" Version="1.1.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="TINS.Native.linux-x64" Version="1.1.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="TINS.Native.osx-x64" Version="1.1.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="TINS.Native.osx-arm64" Version="1.1.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
